# Wave W17-P (Route 118): ford willow — a ford willow in river greens: a broad low crown that DROOPS, its strands hanging past the crown’s edge toward the water it shades, highlight lifted to the crown’s top, on ford turf (ground baked in). Route 118’s own tree — the fleet’s only willow form: split from every elm and pine by the droop itself, and from Route 119’s upright rain pine by posture (the willow leans to the river; the rain pine stands up in the weather).
